From: Artem Pelenitsyn <a.pelenitsyn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:46:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] Keep what is specific to mhs in Distribution.Simple.MHS

So that supporting MicroHs adds as little as possible to the rest of Cabal:

* The errors of mhs become a type of Distribution.Simple.MHS, with its own
  display instance, rather than constructors of CabalException.
* The -D options for the version macros are made in Distribution.Simple.MHS
  from the output of generateCabalMacrosHeader, which is unchanged: every
  #define of the header becomes an option, the first definition of a macro
  winning as in the header.
* reexportedModulesSupported reads the "Support reexported-modules" property
  of any compiler rather than only of GHC, which sets it from its --info, and
  Distribution.Simple.MHS sets it for mhs.

Outside Distribution.Simple.MHS, what remains is an entry per function that
dispatches on the compiler flavour (install, register, the change monitoring
of package databases), the --mhs flag of configure, and the compiler program
of 'cabal path'.

